melody:
# Verse 1
In Dub-lin's fair ci-ty, where girls are so pret-ty, I
D4 G4/ G4. G4 G4/ B4. G4 A4 A4. A4/ A4/ C5. A4
first set my eyes on sweet Mol-ly Ma-lone, as she
B4 A4 G4 D5 C5 B4 B4 A4. G4/ A4(2) D4/ D4/
wheeled her wheel-bar-row through streets broad and nar-row, cry-ing
G4 G4. G4/ G4/ B4. G4 A4 A4. A4/ A4/ C5. A4/ A4/
"Cock-les and mus-sels, a-live, a-live, oh!"
B4/ D5. C5 B4/ D5. C5 B4. G4/ A4 G4(2)

# Chorus
A-live, a-live, oh! A-live, a-live, oh! Cry-ing
D4 G4. G4/ G4 G4/ ~B4. G4 A4. A4/ A4 A4/ ~C5. A4/ A4/
"Cock-les and mus-sels, a-live, a-live, oh!"
B4/ D5. C5 B4/ D5. C5 B4. G4/ A4 G4(2)

# Verse 2
She was a fish-mon-ger, but sure 'twas no won-der, for
D4 G4/ G4. G4 G4/ B4. G4 A4 A4. A4/ A4/ C5. A4
so were her fa-ther and mo-ther be-fore. And they
B4 A4 G4 D5 C5 B4 B4 A4. G4/ A4(2) D4/ D4/
each wheeled their bar-row through streets broad and nar-row, cry-ing
G4 G4. G4/ G4/ B4. G4 A4 A4. A4/ A4/ C5. A4/ A4/
"Cock-les and mus-sels, a-live, a-live, oh!"
B4/ D5. C5 B4/ D5. C5 B4. G4/ A4 G4(2)

# Chorus
A-live, a-live, oh! A-live, a-live, oh! Cry-ing
D4 G4. G4/ G4 G4/ ~B4. G4 A4. A4/ A4 A4/ ~C5. A4/ A4/
"Cock-les and mus-sels, a-live, a-live, oh!"
